- When a button is clicked: show request URL, editable JSON request body, and response JSON
- Allow user to modify request JSON and send again
- Allow user to modify response JSON and set it as a mock response (i.e., send it to a mock endpoint)
- Use Preact and Spectre CSS
- The right pane should keep the existing GetImagePanel and SetMockResponsePanel

---

## My Own Answer

**Approach:**
- Create a reusable `PostApiPanel` component for the left pane.
- It will have buttons for each POST API method (e.g., DetectObjects, FindPosition, etc.).
- When a button is clicked, it sets the POST URI and a default JSON body.
- Show editable fields for the request URL and JSON body.
- Show a "Send" button to POST the request and display the response JSON (editable).
- Show a "Set Mock Response" button to send the edited response JSON to the mock endpoint.
- The right pane remains as in the original code (GetImagePanel and SetMockResponsePanel).
- Integrate this into each Vision tab page.

**Sample implementation outline:**

```js
const PostApiPanel = ({ apiPrefix }) => {
  const methods = [
    { name: "DetectObjects", endpoint: `/api/${apiPrefix}/detectObjects`, defaultBody: { imageUrl: "" } },
    { name: "ClassifyImage", endpoint: `/api/${apiPrefix}/classifyImage`, defaultBody: { imageUrl: "" } },
    { name: "FindPosition", endpoint: `/api/${apiPrefix}/findPosition`, defaultBody: { imageUrl: "", target: "" } },
    // Add more as needed
  ];
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState(null);
  const [postUri, setPostUri] = useState("");
  const [postBody, setPostBody] = useState("");
  const [response, setResponse] = useState("");
  const [mockBody, setMockBody] = useState("");

  const selectMethod = (m) => {
    setSelected(m);
    setPostUri(m.endpoint);
    setPostBody(JSON.stringify(m.defaultBody, null, 2));
    setResponse("");
    setMockBody("");
  };

  const sendPost = async () => {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(postUri, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: postBody,
      });
      const data = await res.json();
      const str = JSON.stringify(data, null, 2);
      setResponse(str);
      setMockBody(str);
    } catch (e) {
      setResponse("Error: " + e.message);
    }
  };

  const setMock = async () => {
    if (!selected) return;
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(mockBody);
      const apiName = selected.name.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + selected.name.slice(1);
      const body = { api: apiName, response: parsed };
      await fetch(`/api/setresponse/${apiPrefix}/${apiName}`, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      });
      alert("Mock response set!");
    } catch (e) {
      alert("Invalid JSON in response field.");
    }
  };

  return html`
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h4 class="panel-title">POST API Methods</h4></div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="btn-group btn-group-block">
          ${methods.map(m => html`
            <button class="btn" onClick=${() => selectMethod(m)}>${m.name}</button>
          `)}
        </div>
        ${selected && html`
          <div>
            <label class="form-label">Request URL</label>
            <input class="form-input" value=${postUri} onInput=${e => setPostUri(e.target.value)} />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="form-label">Request JSON Body</label>
            <textarea class="form-input" rows="4" value=${postBody} onInput=${e => setPostBody(e.target.value)}></textarea>
          </div>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" onClick=${sendPost}>Send</button>
          <div>
            <label class="form-label">Response JSON (editable for mock)</label>
            <textarea class="form-input" rows="4" value=${mockBody} onInput=${e => setMockBody(e.target.value)}></textarea>
          </div>
          <button class="btn btn-success" onClick=${setMock}>Set Mock Response</button>
        `}
      </div>
    </div>
  `;
};
```

Then, in each Vision tab page, use:

```js
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column col-6 col-md-12">
    <${PostApiPanel} apiPrefix=${apiPrefix} />
  </div>
  <div class="column col-6 col-md-12">
    <${GetImagePanel} apiPrefix=${apiPrefix} />
    <${SetMockResponsePanel} apiPrefix=${apiPrefix} />
  </div>
</div>
```

---

## Evaluation of Assistant A

**Strengths:**
- Provides a full, ready-to-use HTML file with all code.
- Implements a `PostApiPanel` component as described in the prompt and my answer.
- Buttons for multiple POST methods, editable request URL/body, response JSON, and a "Set Mock Response" button.
